{"entryId":"1575","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1575:1","sourceSha256":"5a7d436d7dd61a5a0c03d81dad0727f1bfe97f27778cedc4c439246cf29cf561","englishSha256":"6525f19b3a54d511a0249913a1ca7d3c9867525a3af0b3a204f8d05da2eaebef","citations":[{"id":"1575:1:citation-01","he":[0,20],"en":[10,31],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_48b.10"},"reference":"Zevachim 48b:10","assessment":"The Bavli explicitly calls Mar Zutra the son of Rav Tavi. That direction agrees with the translation. The attached author note reverses it. A later exchange on the same folio gives a separate son-of-Mari wording.","evidence":[{"reference":"Zevachim 48b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_48b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Zevachim 48b:28","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_48b.28"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1100:1","target":{"entry":1100,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"The Hebrew and Zevachim both name Tavi as father and Mar Zutra as son. An inherited author note reverses the relationship. The text and translation agree in giving Mar Zutra as the son. Separate the later different patronym on the same daf.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Zevachim 48b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_48b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Zevachim 48b:28","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_48b.28"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1100:1","target":{"entry":1100,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
